# Storm shield — testnet gateway hiding behind a flat plant-wide L2.
#
# wan0 faces the corporate network: one giant broadcast domain, every
# ARP/mDNS/SSDP/NetBIOS frame from the whole site arrives here. Policy:
# kill the firehose at the driver, admit only replies to flows the
# testnet initiated, count what got dropped as evidence.
#
# Known gap: ARP (non-IP) passes the FWL program untouched — the
# kernel needs it for the wan gateway anyway, and FWL has no L2
# fields yet.
#
# SITE EDIT: `10.99.82.1` below is the appliance's own address on the
# testnet, and `10.99.82.255` that segment's directed broadcast. Both
# appear in the lan block. Change them together with system.yaml.

zone wan = [wan0]
zone lan = [lan0]

@xdp(wan)

# --- evidence counters ---
count wan_total
count noise_multicast if pkt.dst_ip in 224.0.0.0/4
count noise_broadcast if pkt.dst_ip == 255.255.255.255
count noise_netbios if pkt.proto == udp
       and (pkt.dst_port == 137 or pkt.dst_port == 138)

# --- keep the wan lease alive (DHCP offers arrive as broadcast) ---
allow if pkt.proto == udp and pkt.src_port == 67 and pkt.dst_port == 68

# --- the plant-floor firehose dies here ---
# mDNS, SSDP, LLMNR, WS-Discovery — all multicast, all dead:
drop if pkt.dst_ip in 224.0.0.0/4
drop if pkt.dst_ip == 255.255.255.255
# NetBIOS name/datagram service arrives as subnet-directed broadcast,
# which looks unicast to us — match the ports instead:
drop if pkt.proto == udp
       and (pkt.dst_port == 137 or pkt.dst_port == 138)
# Site-specific: uncomment with the corporate subnet's directed
# broadcast address once known.
# drop if pkt.dst_ip == 10.1.255.255

# --- flood guard for whatever unicast noise remains ---
drop limited by rate_limit(2000, per=src_ip)

# --- replies to testnet-initiated flows only; nothing else exists ---
# `related` is not optional here. An ICMP error carries no ports, so it
# is never `established`, and the errors this list admits are the ones
# the testnets' OWN outbound flows provoke — above all the frag-needed
# that path-MTU discovery runs on. With `== established` alone, ping
# works, DNS works, and every large transfer hangs with nothing logged
# anywhere (measured on the rig: l11_05).
allow if conntrack(pkt).state in [established, related]

default drop

@xdp(lan)

# THE ORDER OF THIS BLOCK IS THE POLICY. `masquerade` and `redirect to
# wan` are unconditional, so anything that reaches them leaves on the
# uplink wearing the appliance's address — including traffic that was
# never going anywhere, because it was addressed to the appliance
# itself. A DHCP DISCOVER from a testnet client is addressed to
# 255.255.255.255 (it has no address yet, and neither has it learned
# ours); with the two allow rules below missing it was masqueraded and
# broadcast onto the corporate network, arriving on the far side as
#
#     10.99.82.1.68 > 255.255.255.255.67
#
# while this box's own dnsmasq — correctly bound, correctly contained —
# never saw the packet at all. A policy called "storm shield" was
# pumping testnet broadcast into the office. Copy this ordering.

count lan_total

# --- 1. traffic addressed to THIS BOX is delivered to this box ---
# DHCP first, and by port rather than by address: a client with no
# lease cannot address us, so DISCOVER and REBIND arrive as broadcast.
allow if pkt.proto == udp and pkt.dst_port == 67
# ...and everything aimed at the gateway address itself: DNS, NTP, the
# CLI over ssh. `allow` is terminal, so these never reach masquerade.
allow if pkt.dst_ip == 10.99.82.1

# --- 2. the testnet's own noise stays inside the testnet ---
# The wan block above kills the office firehose coming in. This is the
# same rule facing the other way, and it is the half that stops us
# being the storm: mDNS/SSDP/LLMNR, limited and directed broadcast, and
# NetBIOS, none of which is routable and all of which would otherwise
# be masqueraded onto the uplink one frame at a time.
drop if pkt.dst_ip in 224.0.0.0/4
drop if pkt.dst_ip == 255.255.255.255
drop if pkt.dst_ip == 10.99.82.255
drop if pkt.proto == udp
       and (pkt.dst_port == 137 or pkt.dst_port == 138)

# --- 3. only what is left is egress ---
# Testnet egress: hide every inside address behind the wan IP.
count lan_out
masquerade
redirect to wan
